    {
      "sha": "36b35d7c1f056fe7c7b5109fe1141ecd9658f384",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/36b35d7c1f056fe7c7b5109fe1141ecd9658f384",
      "message": "Assign the ordinary PR runtime matrix to Node CI\n\nKeep focused local regressions, fast hooks and distinct acceptance lanes required. Retain explicit full-local execution and conservative fallback when hosted routing cannot be established. Add the two missing hosted typechecks before moving matrix ownership.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-07T03:38:41Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "16d43facec1b14304944c0a8554fefdf8249c4b9",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/16d43facec1b14304944c0a8554fefdf8249c4b9",
      "message": "Ratchet the scanner test size cap after removing its coverage debt\n\nRepo Tools CI on 8bbbeb2d1 refused the stale exact cap: recorded 708, actual 705. Lower only this cap and its declaration count, and point the scanner comment at the replacement suite.\n\nnode --test demo/scripts/lib/module-sizes.test.mjs: 1 passed, 0 failed, exit 0 on 2026-10-07; before correction 1 passed and 1 process failure, exit 1. Verified all 360 explicit caps. No executable source or assertion changes.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-07T03:26:04Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "8bbbeb2d1a02a8e12d20b8393ca939737998cebd",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/8bbbeb2d1a02a8e12d20b8393ca939737998cebd",
      "message": "Refuse contradictory status observations at immutable outputs\n\nCompare the full StateQueueStatusV1 identity at repeated live outputs before accepting the scan. Constructor and same-kind field disagreements were silently accepted by the scanner; signed decisions already had a later quarantine check. Reuse the integrity refusal and durable quarantine path.\n\nTerminal retention records carry forward an older datum while naming a newer spent output, so exclude those synthetic observations. The replay-produced control caught this false positive in review.\n\nFocused recipe: 82 passed, no selected skips, 40 filtered assertions, exit 0 on 2026-10-07. Receipt ed80cdb0-c4b2-40f3-93ba-9796f7af9f84. Guard-removal control: 4 passed, 16 failed, exit 1. Refs #645.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-07T03:17:00Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "6c14d1011a9896f4bb7bfb7e70fa0423a86907f5",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/6c14d1011a9896f4bb7bfb7e70fa0423a86907f5",
      "message": "Add status disagreement observation regressions (#645)\n\nExercise immutable-output status contradictions through the scanner and committee peer boundary. The scanner matrix is regression-first: four agreement controls pass and twelve disagreements resolve instead of refusing on the canonical base. The new file keeps the existing scanner test line budget intact. Repair and final verification follow in this draft.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-07T03:10:17Z"
    },
